  "body": "Stacked on #4164 (merge #4164 first).\n\n## What changed\n\n- A machine file can state a new optional key, `controller.work_offset_max`. It is the highest work offset that the control holds. On a Heidenhain control it is the last row of the preset table.\n- The machine reader and the raw post engine refuse a value that is not a whole number from 1 to 255. The message names the key.\n- The key is an installation fact, the same as `tooling.max_tool_number` (#4164). The mirror carries it.\n- The post engine refuses a `PARAM WorkOffset` above the key. The refusal names the setup and the key. It comes before any script hook runs, so it applies to each post.\n- `fehlmann-picomax55.mch` states `\"work_offset_max\": 5`. Its description tells the shop to check the preset table at the control.\n- `assets/machines/AGENTS.md` documents the key.\n- A machine without the key keeps the post's own limit. A key above the post's own limit does not raise that limit.\n\n## Cause\n\n- Both Heidenhain posts accept presets 1..6 (`workOffsetMax = 6`).\n- The Picomax preset table on the 2008 delivery CD (`PRESET.PR`) has rows 0..5 only (`docs/research/heidenhain/picomax-55-review.md`, defect 14).\n- `Q339=+6` names a row that does not exist. The control stops with an alarm.\n- The machine file had no place to state the row count.\n\nThe refusal is a hard error, not a counted warning. A counted warning was not enough: the Klartext post throws \"missing or unsupported preset (WorkOffset)\" when the engine holds back the offset, and that error hid the warning.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins, in the `heidenhain_cycles` directory suite (new submodule `heidenhain_cycles/preset_rows.rs`, no new test binary):\n\n- `preset_rows::heidenhain_posts_refuse_a_preset_above_the_machine_preset_table`: preset 5 posts with no warning, and preset 6 is refused with `setup Setup1: uses work offset 6` and `controller.work_offset_max`. It runs both posts on the raw file and on the parsed mirror.\n- `preset_rows::an_unstated_or_larger_machine_maximum_keeps_the_post_limit`: no machine posts preset 6; a key of 99 posts preset 6 and refuses 7 with \"work offsets 1-6 only\".\n- `preset_rows::a_malformed_work_offset_max_is_refused_by_name`: 0, -1, 2.5, \"5\" and 256 are refused by the reader and by the raw engine.\n\nRed before the fix: yes. On the unchanged code the test did not compile (no `Machine::work_offset_max`). With the two field assertions taken out, all three tests failed: preset 6 posted, and no value was refused.\n\nMutations (each one red, then restored and green):\n\n- Engine guard disabled: `heidenhain_posts_refuse_a_preset_above_the_machine_preset_table` red.\n- Mirror line disabled: the same test red (mirrored input).\n- Reader range widened to 256: `a_malformed_work_offset_max_is_refused_by_name` red.\n\nGate on the final head:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on `9d6ebbd62`: 343 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (29.3 min). The plan included each app suite that reads `heidenhain.cps`, `klartext_builtin`, `machine_controller` and the example catalog suites.\n- Then a clippy fix (`b3541f715`, the guard as one `if let`). `cargo xtask gate quick --base HEAD~1` on the final head: 13 steps, 0 failed. It ran `post suites: lib`, `work_offset_index`, `example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive`, `example_catalog_edge_work` and the first-part suites.\n- `cargo xtask gate test preset_rows --crate post --binary heidenhain_cycles` on the final head: green.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- The light lane was not run. Its dry run shows only the motion adaptive and pocket twins. This diff does not change them.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The example catalog suites and the quick plan ran green. `git diff --stat` against #4164's head shows no `*.nc`, `*.cl` or `examples/catalog/**` change.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The row count was not checked at the control. The value 5 comes from the 2008 CD. The issue's first \"Done means\" item stays with the maintainer. If the shop added rows, raise the key in the machine file.\n- The setup's work offset list in the UI still offers offsets up to the post's limit. The post refusal blocks the wrong program. Display is a possible follow-up.\n- An older app reads a project from this build and drops the key (no `deny_unknown_fields` on `Machine`), so it keeps the post's own limit. This is the same as for #4164.\n- No UI change, so no screenshots.\n- No heavy step: this is a `P3` PR (AGENTS.md \"Heavy lanes at review\").\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #4164: same lines (`FACT_KEYS`, the `Machine` fields, `parse_mch_with`, `checked_input`, `mirror`). This PR is stacked on it.\n- #4161: touches `def.rs`, `parse.rs` and `machine_installation.rs`, in other fields and functions. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n- #3982: touches `assets/machines/AGENTS.md`, another section. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: A machine file can state `controller.work_offset_max`, the last preset row of the control; the post refuses a higher work offset by setup name, and the Fehlmann Picomax 55 states 5.\n\nFixes #4088\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
